IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`
IMPORT `ma-nouns`
IMPORT `ma-reading`

-- Tests for ma-reading.l4.  Expected values are written from the Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) as the
-- copied module quotes it ("person" and "party" include any company or association or body of persons,
-- corporate or unincorporate; "court" means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore).

§ `Tests -- the Act's words`

-- The copied table says what kind of definition each word has (expected from the Interpretation Act's words above).
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "person" EQUALS JUST Includes
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "party" EQUALS JUST Includes
#ASSERT `the kind of definition of` "court" EQUALS JUST Means
-- A word that the Interpretation Act's s 2(1) does not define has no entry.
#ASSERT `the definition of` "misrepresentation" EQUALS NOTHING

-- "person" and "party" include a company, an association and a body of persons: each named in the entry.
#ASSERT `ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `A company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `An association` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `Another body of persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "include" does not close the list and names no individual: not covered, NOTHING (never FALSE).
#ASSERT `ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `An individual` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 1 to 3 "person" and "party" include the party (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `Something else` EQUALS NOTHING

-- "court" means any court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore: a "means" definition says no to the rest.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the body is a "court" (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `A court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the body is a "court" (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `Any other court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the body is a "court" (Interpretation Act s 2(1))` `Any other body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
